# The crates at the foot of the stair, under the Iron Brand keep (Act 3).
# Opens on approach (CompProperties_TSC_ProximityDialogue) and by right-click
# afterwards. The company's answer to surfacing in a fully manned keep: make
# a noise, fight the half that comes down here, climb into a thinner keep.
#
# The scene only MAKES the plan (and rolls the rigging). The push itself is
# a separate right-click order on the crates (JobDriver_TSC_TipCrates), so
# the company takes positions first and the noise starts on the player's
# word, not when the dialogue closes.
#
# {PLAYER} is the one who walked up and spotted it.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_CellarCrates

# Once the plan is made, reopening the scene must not re-roll the Thievery
# check or re-plan; it just points at the waiting order.
entry armed if flag(TSC_KeepCratesPlanned)
# The lone-adventurer start has nobody to say it out loud to, so the scene
# has a solo variant rather than a companion talking to an empty corridor.
entry alone if party_size(<2)

== start ==
Barrels and crates, stacked four high against the wall where the stair goes up. Salt fish, by the smell, and something that was flour once. The Brand puts its stores where its stores have always gone.

{PLAYER} stops walking. Looks at the stack. Looks up the stair. Looks back at the stack.

"How thin do you want them," {PLAYER} says, "before we go up there?"

* "Go on." -> plan
* "We go up quiet. Leave it." -> end

== plan ==
"That lot comes down with a crash you could hear in Thornden. And what's at the top of these steps is a keep full of men who have never once in five years had to wonder what a noise in the cellar meant."

A hand on the top crate. Not pushing yet.

"So they send some down. Not all of them, they're not fools, but some. And they come down a stone stair into a dark corridor, in ones and twos, into us." A shrug. "It's not clever. It's just numbers. Every one that dies down here isn't up there when we come out."

* "Do it." -> ready
    check Thievery 8 -> rigged | ready
* "Too loud. We take our chances above." -> end

== ready ==
"Then it goes over on your word." A hand flat against the crate that will start it, not pushing yet.

"Put everyone where you want them standing when the Brand comes down that stair. Then give the word."

* [Take positions first.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_KeepCratesPlanned)

== rigged ==
{PLAYER} spends a minute on it first: a barrel set on its shoulder against the stack, a line of twine, the whole thing balanced to go over on one pull from a safe corner.

"Rigged. They will arrive to a room that is already ours. Put everyone where you want them, then give the word."

* [Take positions first.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_KeepCratesPlanned); flag(TSC_KeepCratesRigged)

== alone ==
Barrels and crates, stacked four high against the wall where the stair goes up. Salt fish, by the smell, and something that was flour once.

{PLAYER} looks at the stack, and up the stair, and at the stack again, and works out the thing nobody is there to argue with.

That lot goes over with a crash they will hear at the top. Some of them come down to see. Not all - they are not fools - but some. And they come down a stone stair into a dark corridor, in ones and twos.

Alone, that is either the best idea available or the last one. There is no third opinion coming.

* [Set it up.] -> ready_alone
    check Thievery 8 -> rigged_alone | ready_alone
* [Leave it. Go up quiet.] -> end

== ready_alone ==
The stack stays standing, one crate worked loose at the shoulder, a shove away from loud.

Find the angle first. Then the noise.

* [Take a position first.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_KeepCratesPlanned)

== rigged_alone ==
A minute of work: a barrel set on its shoulder against the stack, a line of twine, the whole thing balanced to go over on one pull from a safe corner.

They will arrive to a corridor that is already an ambush. Pick the corner first.

* [Take a position first.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_KeepCratesPlanned); flag(TSC_KeepCratesRigged)

== armed ==
The stack stands where it was left: one push from loud, the plan already made. It only wants the word.

* [Not yet.] -> end
